      }
    },
    {
      "name": "James Blackstone",
      "role": "social_historian",
      "description": "Prof. James Blackstone \u2014 a legal historian who specializes in Victorian institutions.  Brings the real-world context \u2014 what Chancery actually was, how the Poor Law worked, what it meant to be Jo.  Can get genuinely angry about injustice, past and present.  Connects Dickens' world to modern parallels without being heavy-handed about it.  Dry wit.",
      "voice_policy": {
        "rate": 0.96,
